Set \code{wbic_weight} in \code{\link[=joinpoint]{joinpoint()}} before fitting to choose the candidate
Weight/WBIC numerical method; extraction never changes the cached scores.

For \code{k} joinpoints and \code{n} observations, \code{n_parameters = 2*k + 2} and
\code{model_df = n - n_parameters}. The fixed-grid continuous regression has
\code{k + 2} coefficients and its own \code{fixed_grid_df}. NCI-style coefficient
inference removes observations at joinpoints and fits unconstrained segment
lines to estimate covariance, giving a third, separate \code{inference_df}.
Coefficient point estimates still come from the continuous fitted model.
Intercepts refer to time zero on the log-outcome scale.

Failed groups remain in \code{data} and \code{statistics}, with missing fitted
statistics, no coefficient/candidate rows, and \code{NULL} matrix entries.
If fitting succeeds but inference fails, coefficient estimates are retained
with missing inference fields and status \code{"inference_failed"}.
Missing or infinite t statistics follow the conventions of \code{\link[=calc_apc]{calc_apc()}}.

The coefficient calculations share the package's covariance-whitening path
for correlated errors. Agreement with NCI 6.1.0 has been checked for the
bundled independent-error \code{jp_data} cohort-zero selected model, not for all
error structures or all candidate scores. Extraction does not change the
existing fitting, EQ, or parametric algorithms. APC/AAPC interval tables
remain available through \code{\link[=calc_apc]{calc_apc()}} and \code{\link[=calc_aapc]{calc_aapc()}}.
